STATEMENT OF CHANGES (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
----------------------------------------------

Relative to nunchaku 1.2.1, the vendored file has been changed to:

  * incorporate upstream PR #926, adding FLUX.2-klein support that was not
    present in the 1.2.1 release;
  * route attention through an unfused QKV path so that a runtime hook can
    observe the projections (upstream fuses QKV inside a single call, so a
    hook never fires) -- see route_b/README.md;
  * accommodate a widened `x_embedder` (128 -> 256 input channels) for this
    project's glyph-latent conditioning channel.

These modifications were made by this repository's author and are not
endorsed by, or the responsibility of, the Nunchaku project.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------

Apache-2.0 section 4 requires that anyone redistributing a derivative work
(a) hand recipients a copy of the licence, (b) carry prominent notices
stating that files were changed, and (c) retain the original attribution
notices. Until 2026-08-08 this repository shipped the derived file with none
of the three -- provenance was described in route_b/README.md as prose, which
documents the code but does not satisfy the licence.

Note that the Route B track itself is CLOSED (see route_b/README.md and
CLAUDE.md): Nunchaku exposes no runtime-LoRA API for the quantized FLUX.2
transformer. The code is retained as a record of the investigation, which
does not change the redistribution obligation.
